                <pb facs="0989" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v21/pg946"/>

                <head>366. Memorandum From the Chief of the Western Hemisphere Division, Directorate
                    of Operations, Central Intelligence Agency (Phillips) to the Executive Secretary
                    of the 40 Committee (Ratliffe)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d366-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1973-09-25">September 25,
                        1973</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Cancellation of 20 August 1973 40 Committee Approval</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. On 20 August 1973 the 40 Committee approved $1,000 for support of Chilean
                    political parties and private sector organizations opposed to the Allende
                    regime. The military coup of 11 September 1973 changed the situation in Chile so
                    completely that we no longer consider the 20 August 1973 40 Committee approval
                    to be valid.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d366-f2"/></p>
                <p>2. In due course we intend to submit a new memorandum for the 40 Committee
                    describing proposed new political and covert action operations in Chile.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_PDA_1">David A. Phillips<anchor n="3" xml:id="d366-f3"
                        /></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
